# Environment Variables Template
# INSTRUCTIONS: Copy this file to .env.local and fill in your actual values
# Command (PowerShell): Copy-Item .env.example .env.local
# Command (bash):       cp .env.example .env.local
#
# After creating or editing .env.local, restart the dev server (pnpm run dev).
# Cloudflare production uses Dashboard env vars — local dev needs .env.local.

# Supabase Configuration
# Get these values from: https://app.supabase.com/project/_/settings/api
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-id.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key-here

# IMPORTANT NOTES:
# 1. The .env.local file is in .gitignore and will NOT be committed to git
# 2. Never commit real credentials to version control
# 3. The NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY is a publishable key (safe to use client-side)
# 4. Your data is protected by Row-Level Security (RLS) policies in Supabase
